<title>BAHRAIN: Bahrain BMB lifts 96 net profit to $9.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Bahrain BMB lifts 96 net profit to $9.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(millions of U.S. dollars)</p>
<p> Net profit		  9.5   vs     5.6</p>
<p> Operating income	 24.9   vs    16.8</p>
<p> Net operating income   15.8   vs     8.0</p>
<p> Loan loss provision     2.4   vs     NIL</p>
<p> Investment provision    2.6   vs     2.2</p>
<p> Shareholders funds    106.7   vs    98.2</p>
<p> Customer deposits     112.1   vs   129.6</p>
<p> Assets		    645.9   vs   454.1</p>
<p>Full Name: Bahrain Middle East Bank E.C.</p>
<p>Note - BMB, set up in 1982, is 28.6 percent owned by Burgan Bank SAK of Kuwait. The rest is held by investors in the Gulf.</p>
</text>
